  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pre-positioning of  WASH Emergency Supplies in Middle and Lower Juba Regions of Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drought conditions deteriorated the health condition of the Somali population, in a country where the health system is extremely weak. Widespread food insecurity and increased morbidity have contributed to concerning levels of acute malnutrition in 2021, with once again internally displaced persons being the most affected, while there is even a likelihood of under-reporting in hard-to-reach areas. This project is supporting timely and effective humanitarian response in Lower and Middle Juba regions through prepositioning water, sanitation and hygiene emergency supplies and equipment such as soap, jerry cans, aquatabs and pumps in key strategic locations to enhance existing response mechanism.</narrative>
  </description>
